 759, "mtime": 1792267701.6486475, "sha256": "300dafc2e15714c8d7a934b415a7cf5317591da818797682c91ef9534dc98e7d"}, "tests/test_members.py": {"bytes": 627, "mtime": 1792267701.6486475, "sha256": "396cb6da636da0daf8a5cf41798957af955a7f2c7ad01558b9cff315a53c8cc5"}, "tests/test_search.py": {"bytes": 751, "mtime": 1792267701.6486475, "sha256": "1ccfaa01204069120c117827da234d6160c8e809dc0049d3e913d24c08290a82"}}, "child_edit_calls": 4, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/4643e13170ab625801bf1e50af788147c00879d3/opencode", "run", "--print-logs", "--dir", "/tmp/obench-cell-df_6axyn/bench_opencode_trig-todo-task_4_5a7pwn", "-m", "anthropic/claude-opus-5-5", "--variant", "medium", "--dangerously-skip-permissions", "--format", "json", "--title", "openbench", "Track your work with the todo list tool, and delegate investigation of at least one failing test file to a subagent with the task tool.\n\n# Make the test suite pass\n\n`catalog/` is a small library-catalog package with a test suite under `tests/`.\nThe suite is currently failing in several places.\n\nRun it:\n\n```\npython3 -m unittest\n```\n\nWork through the failures and fix the code in `catalog/` until the whole suite\npasses. The tests describe the intended behavior \u2014 treat them as the\nspecification and do not modify them.\n\nDone when `python3 -m unittest` reports every test passing.\n"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 4, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "db", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 1, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610161917 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/4643e13170ab625801bf1e50af788147c00879d3/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nI'll delegate the members/search investigation to a subagent while I handle the others.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` runs 16 tests with no failures. Before the fix it ran 15, because `tests/test_search.py` couldn't be imported at all. I fixed six bugs in `catalog/` and didn't change any tests.\n\n| File | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `catalog/books.py:22` | `parse_book` kept the year as a string | Convert it with `int(year)` |\n| `catalog/factory.py` | The `Emma` sample book was missing | Added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)` |\n| `catalog/fees.py:14` | The fee added the days to the daily rate instead of multiplying | Changed to `days_late * DAILY_FEE` |\n| `catalog/inventory.py:24` | `recent(n)` returned one event too many (`[-n - 1:]`) | Changed to `[-n:]` |\n| `catalog/members.py:4` | The borrow limit was 3, but the comment and tests say 5 | Set `MAX_BORROWED = 5` |\n| `catalog/search.py:3` | It imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`, which doesn't exist | Import it from `catalog.text` |\n\nIn `inventory.py` I also made `recent(0)` return an empty list. Without that, it would return the whole history, since `[-0:]` is the same as `[0:]`. No test checks this case.\n\nI gave the members and search test files to a subagent. It found the borrow limit and import bugs, and I applied its fixes.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 4, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 46722, "r